  ],
  "intro": "Service NSW has a number of policies under which it operates. These policies relate to internal and external operational procedures and protocols and are listed in the Policy Document Register.\n\nThese documents are used by Service NSW in connection with the exercise of functions that may affect or may be of interest to the public.\n\nIn accordance with the Government Information (Public Access) Act 2009 (GIPA Act), the Department of Customer Service has made a number of policies, procedures and guidance documents publicly available, free of charge, including:\n\nTo access a copy of any of these documents or if there is a policy document you would like to request but is not on this list, please call the GIPA team on (02) 9219 3700 or email gipa@customerservice.nsw.gov.au\n\nService NSW is an executive agency of the Department of Customer Service (DCS). Further information about DCS policies can be found on the DCS Policy document register.",
